{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet5C6biE3scrv1zXDjeo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have all the context I need:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment feature: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/`\n  - `Shipment.kt:9-14` defines the data class with status property\n  - `Shipment.kt:23-27` defines ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n  - `ShipmentController.kt:26-56` handles POST /shipments (create) and GET operations\n  - `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-18` has save() and findById() methods\n- Error handling: `ApiExceptions.kt:11-24` defines ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- Error codes: `ApiError.kt:31-37` defines the ErrorCode enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses for errors; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError envelope\n- Response body for errors: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}}`\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions for both success and error bodies\n- Tests reset state in @BeforeEach and use request builders (post(), get()) helper methods\n- Similar patterns in OrderController and ShipmentController\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — add new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` — add new error code `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` for the 409 conflict case\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add tests for confirm endpoint covering all cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if shipment state is inadvertently modified\n- Incorrect error code could break API contract\n- Missing idempotency could fail on retry case\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone identified; the requirement fully specifies all four cases and their outcomes.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add error code `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum. This represents the 409 conflict when trying to confirm a cancelled shipment. (1 line addition)\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by id (throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return it as-is (idempotent success)\n   - If status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED, save, and return it\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\n   - Return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.OK).body(updated)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED`\n   - `confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing` (idempotent)\n   - `confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code`\n   - `confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code`\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- *Could add a separate service layer with business logic* — Rejected because existing controllers (OrderController, ShipmentController) have no service layer and directly manipulate repository. Keeping consistency with existing architecture.\n- *Could use a generic error code like VALIDATION_FAILED* — Rejected because the code exists for a state conflict (CANCELLED status), not validation. The SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code is precise and follows the pattern of SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND (status-based codes).\n- *Could make confirm idempotent in a different way* — The requirement specifies \"succeeds and changes nothing\" which is the idempotent pattern; no update needed if already CONFIRMED.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Repository read | State check | Action | Repository write | Response | Status |\n|------|-------|-----------------|-------------|--------|------------------|----------|--------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | /shipments/S-1/confirm | findById → Shipment(status=CREATED) | status == CREATED | update to CONFIRMED | save(Shipment(...CONFIRMED)) | Shipment(...CONFIRMED) | 200 OK |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED | /shipments/S-1/confirm | findById → Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | status == CONFIRMED | no-op | (none) | same Shipment | 200 OK |\n| CANCELLED → error | /shipments/S-1/confirm | findById → Shipment(status=CANCELLED) | status == CANCELLED | throw ConflictException | (none) | ApiError(SHIPMENT_CANCELLED) | 409 Conflict |\n| Not found → error | /shipments/S-missing/confirm | findById → null | not reached | throw ResourceNotFoundException | (none) | ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) | 404 Not Found |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test 1: confirm_CREATED_to_CONFIRMED** — Create S-1 in CREATED status, POST /shipments/S-1/confirm, assert 200 OK and status field is CONFIRMED\n2. **Test 2: confirm_CONFIRMED_is_idempotent** — Create S-2 in CONFIRMED status (via direct repository write since no confirm endpoint yet), POST /shipments/S-2/confirm twice, both should succeed with 200 OK and no state change\n3. **Test 3: confirm_CANCELLED_returns_409** — Write CANCELLED shipment directly to repository, POST /shipments/S-3/confirm, assert 409 Conflict and error.code is SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\n4. **Test 4: confirm_nonexistent_returns_404** — POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm, assert 404 Not Found and error.code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2556,"cache_read_input_tokens":18730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2556},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a59fad6-4c67-4d16-9e15-8a9507e5b37c","uuid":"42e489b9-5944-42e8-8740-0e5822133d76","time